# Cloudflare Pages reads this file to attach HTTP response headers per path.
# Syntax: a path pattern on its own line, followed by indented `Header-Name: value`
# lines that apply to every response matching it. Docs:
# https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/
#
# This file is NOT covered by `npm run build` or any test in this repo. A wrong
# value here does not fail CI — it fails silently in the browser: the disallowed
# script/style/font/request is just dropped, and the only trace is a
# Content-Security-Policy violation line in the DevTools console. Verify any
# change here against a real deployed preview and check the console, not just
# by re-running the test suite.
#
# connect-src is the full list of origins the deployed app talks to, checked
# against the production bundle on 2026-10-01 (Task 185 / B2):
#   *.supabase.co          REST, auth, Edge Functions and the reports bucket
#   openapi.twse.com.tw    TWSE list — `twMarketData.ts` falls back to a direct
#   www.tpex.org.tw        TPEx list — fetch when the Edge proxy fails, so both
#                          are reached from the browser in production, not only
#                          server-side
# It used to carry `https:` and `http://localhost:*` for a user-supplied AI
# provider base URL. That feature is gone — `schema.sql` drops `ai_provider`,
# `ai_base_url` and `ai_api_key`, and no AI code is left in `src/` — so the
# wildcard only widened where injected script could send data.
#
# Deliberately absent: `wss:`. supabase-js ships a realtime client, but nothing
# here subscribes to a channel. If a realtime feature is ever added, its socket
# will be blocked until `wss://*.supabase.co` is added back.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src 'self' data: https://fonts.gstatic.com; img-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' https://*.supabase.co https://openapi.twse.com.tw https://www.tpex.org.tw; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'
